  "body": "Finish parsing the children of XML empty-element tags\n\nWhen the XML parser inserts an element represented by an empty-element tag, immediately finish parsing its children. For a script element, perform the microtask checkpoint and prepare the script when the parser parses its end tag or inserts its empty-element tag. Aborting the parser or encountering a well-formedness error does not trigger script preparation.\n\n- [ ] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed). No explicit positions recorded yet.\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed at https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/65431. The two XHTML subtests cover `loadedmetadata` on `<audio/>` and `<video/>`.\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are unnecessary for the existing behavior, as discussed in [review](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/13265#issuecomment-6982734168).\n- [x] Corresponding [HTML AAM](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/) and [ARIA in HTML](https://w3c.github.io/html-aria/) issues and PRs are unnecessary. This change affects XML parser timing.\n- [x] An [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is unnecessary. The change specifies existing behavior.\n- [x] The top of this description includes a [commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md).\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's